From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] video, joystick: bareapp drivers for the games of bare_app

bare_app, the launcher of the OdroidLinux SDK, starts each game as a
program of its own and hands it a socket and shared memory as
descriptors 3 and 4 (bare_app's src/games/game_ipc.h and its game side
game_ipc_client.h, copied next to the drivers at build time with the
gamepad names of core/input.h). With these drivers an SDL game runs
under bare_app unchanged:

- video "bareapp": picked by itself when the descriptors are there (and
  SDL_VIDEODRIVER names no other driver). The desktop mode is the size of
  bare_app's video layer; a window of any size is fitted to it (aspect
  kept, black borders; SDL_BAREAPP_SCALE=stretch|integer, filtered
  linearly or SDL_BAREAPP_FILTER=nearest, whole multiples always
  nearest). Window surfaces and the software renderer are copied into the
  frame; OpenGL (ES) draws off screen into a pbuffer of the window's size
  on Mesa's surfaceless platform (the GPU's render node, no display) and
  is read back at each swap. Frames are paced to SDL_BAREAPP_FPS (60) as
  a vsync would. bare_app's buttons become keys as SDL_BAREAPP_KEYS says
  ("a=return, b=escape, up=up"); when bare_app goes away the game gets
  SDL_QUIT.
- joystick "bareapp": the gamepad as one game controller with its own
  mapping (buttons by label, F1 start, F2 back...; SDL_BAREAPP_GAMEPAD
  changes it), the left stick, the right one where there is one, L2 and
  R2 as triggers. It switches the Linux driver off with the new hint
  SDL_JOYSTICK_LINUX=0: the evdev devices are the same buttons.

configure: --enable-bareapp (Linux only), also in the generated
configure so that the package needs no autoreconf.

Upstream: not applicable (SDK-specific)
Signed-off-by: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
